<title>USA: Maryland Gov urges more talks on sale of shipyard.</title>
<headline>Maryland Gov urges more talks on sale of shipyard.</headline>
<dateline>DUNDALK, Md. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hundreds of workers at the Bethlehem Steel Corp shipyard in Sparrow's Point, Md., could out of a job, but Gov Parris Glendening is urging more talks.</p>
<p>Glendening urged Peter Angelos, owner of the Baltimore Orioles baseball team, and Bethlehem Steel to continue talks on the sale of the shipyard.</p>
<p>Bethlehem Steel announced Friday that negotiations have stalled. Angelos has offered to buy the yard, but said he does not want to be held responsible for past environmental pollution.</p>
<p>Bethlehmen Steel said it now plans to close the shipyard.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
